(3277526, 453469, 56797, '<td valign="top">What''s weird to me with this shot is that I can''t tell what they are being held up in. silly putty?, playdoh? It''s not clear and that''s confusing. Also the pinkish tones take attention away from the matches which aren''t sharp enough. your D.O.F. is just too shallow at 3.2, with a static subject you should be able to get the aperature up providing you have a tripod. If not I suggest getting one. The colors look oversaturated as well. Which in general is a good thing on DPC but with this you''ve gone just a bit too far.<br/> <br/>HTH</td>', 'What''s weird to me with this shot is that I can''t tell what they are being held up in. silly putty?, playdoh? It''s not clear and that''s confusing. Also the pinkish tones take attention away from the matches which aren''t sharp enough. your D.O.F. is just too shallow at 3.2, with a static subject you should be able to get the aperature up providing you have a tripod. If not I suggest getting one. The colors look oversaturated as well. Which in general is a good thing on DPC but with this you''ve gone just a bit too far. HTH', '2007-01-24 20:46:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(3278699, 453675, 46336, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club. </b> <br/> <br/>Hi Ran,<br/> <br/>Welcome to DPC. I wish you all the best. <br/> <br/>Seems that most of the voters didn''t go for your grainy take on this subject. I think the main problem though is that in a challenge like this where there are so many buring matchstick based submissions you need a really special, creative submission to do well. What might be useful to you is to take the time to really review the top 20 or so entries. <br/> <br/>For myself, I like the grain in your shot. It makes it different to all the other crisp, sharp flames out there. It would have been dead useful to see your post-processing steps so that I could understand what you chose to do to achieve this look. I personally would have loved to see more orange in the flames - best place to get this done is in your white-balance (easiest when shooting in RAW). The fact that none of your matchsticks are cricply in focus I think hit you badly - it makes it difficult to work out exactly where your main subject is. <br/> <br/>It is my hope that these insights are helpful and constructive. Please feel free to PM me if you have any questions regarding this critique. And please remember to mark it "Helpful" if you found it so. Good luck with future challenges. <br/> <br/>Cheers<br/>Paul</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club.   Hi Ran, Welcome to DPC. I wish you all the best.  Seems that most of the voters didn''t go for your grainy take on this subject. I think the main problem though is that in a challenge like this where there are so many buring matchstick based submissions you need a really special, creative submission to do well. What might be useful to you is to take the time to really review the top 20 or so entries.  For myself, I like the grain in your shot. It makes it different to all the other crisp, sharp flames out there. It would have been dead useful to see your post-processing steps so that I could understand what you chose to do to achieve this look. I personally would have loved to see more orange in the flames - best place to get this done is in your white-balance (easiest when shooting in RAW). The fact that none of your matchsticks are cricply in focus I think hit you badly - it makes it difficult to work out exactly where your main subject is.  It is my hope that these insights are helpful and constructive. Please feel free to PM me if you have any questions regarding this critique. And please remember to mark it "Helpful" if you found it so. Good luck with future challenges.  CheersPaul', '2007-01-24 23:42:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(3278864, 452451, 40106, '<td valign="top">oooooh man!!!!  this is soooo cooool!!!  the way he''s totally pointing out the way they''re matching.  i wonder if they called each other the night before and planned to both wear orange.  haha i totally used to do that with my friends!!!! :)  TOO COOL FOR SCHOOL!</td>', 'oooooh man!!!!  this is soooo cooool!!!  the way he''s totally pointing out the way they''re matching.  i wonder if they called each other the night before and planned to both wear orange.  haha i totally used to do that with my friends!!!! :)  TOO COOL FOR SCHOOL!', '2007-01-24 23:51:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(3279126, 452451, 48228, '<td valign="top">Yep, I regonise him for sure.... I like it, as it is a fun image mate.....</td>', 'Yep, I regonise him for sure.... I like it, as it is a fun image mate.....', '2007-01-25 00:08:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(3279190, 454326, 52549, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on top 10 with this excellent and very underrated shot, Ursula.</td>', 'Congratulations on top 10 with this excellent and very underrated shot, Ursula.', '2007-01-25 00:35:13.000000', NULL, 0),
