(3288285, 453675, 69186, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the comments and the Critique Paul. <br/>I wanted to capture a sence for the heat and texture in the match when it''s lit. <br/>So I set the aparture to 3,5 and put the matches in a row, a bent one so I would only get the second one in focus.<br/>My choice was to dhow the detail in the matches, not the fire becouse this is the way I saw it when I lit it.<br/>And It''s not at all grainy, I only used ISO200 and did not push it up in PS afterwards, only changed the white balance in the RAW file. <br/>And since DPC only allows a limited sieze of each picture I had to drop the detail and got some grain insted...<br/></td>', 'Thanks for the comments and the Critique Paul. I wanted to capture a sence for the heat and texture in the match when it''s lit. So I set the aparture to 3,5 and put the matches in a row, a bent one so I would only get the second one in focus.My choice was to dhow the detail in the matches, not the fire becouse this is the way I saw it when I lit it.And It''s not at all grainy, I only used ISO200 and did not push it up in PS afterwards, only changed the white balance in the RAW file. And since DPC only allows a limited sieze of each picture I had to drop the detail and got some grain insted...', '2007-01-26 18:10:36.000000', NULL, 0),
